/T (Method overriding occurs when a subclass provides its own implementation of a method already defined in the superclass. It enables runtime polymorphism, where a parent class reference can refer to different child class objects and invoke the appropriate overridden method. Here, calculateSalary\(\) is overridden by both Manager and Programmer to display their respective salary details. Using parent class references demonstrates dynamic method dispatch and makes the program flexible and reusable. )
/E (Method overriding occurs when a subclass provides its own implementation of a method already defined in the superclass. It enables runtime polymorphism, where a parent class reference can refer to different child class objects and invoke the appropriate overridden method. Here, calculateSalary\(\) is overridden by both Manager and Programmer to display their respective salary details. Using parent class references demonstrates dynamic method dispatch and makes the program flexible and reusable. )
