/T (and provide their own implementations of the calculateSalary\(\) method. By using Employee references to create subclass objects, the program shows how Java selects the appropriate overridden method at runtime. The different salary calculations for the Manager and Programmer confirm that method overriding provides flexibility and allows each employee type to have its own salary calculation. Thus, the program effectively demonstrates the practical use of important Object-Oriented Programming concepts in Java. )
